cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ActiStruct: Active Learning for DFT-Guided Materials Discovery"
message: "If you use ActiStruct, please cite this software."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Khandaker"
    given-names: "Md. Rifat"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0520-4654"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-04"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rifat19R/ActiStruct"
abstract: "ActiStruct is an active-learning workflow for DFT-guided materials
  discovery. It combines a SchNet-style GNN encoder with a frozen-embedding GP
  surrogate (HybridGPSurrogate), an autonomous Quantum ESPRESSO fault-recovery
  engine, a multi-fidelity Ti3C2-O MXene HER oracle, and a Streamlit monitoring
  dashboard. The v0.x reliability-aware layer (QE parser, failure-risk classifier,
  failure-aware LCB acquisition) is retained."
keywords:
  - inverse-design
  - active-learning
  - dft
  - quantum-espresso
  - ase
  - gaussian-process
  - bayesian-optimization
  - gnn
  - schnet
  - multi-fidelity
  - materials-science
  - mxene
